'' A UNION IN AN INITIALISER takes ONE value, for its first alternative, and the rest of its bytes
'' are zeroed -- named or anonymous, with an anonymous struct as an alternative (fbc's
'' dim/union-init.bas, 272 failing asserts before). Expected output is fbc-modern's.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: -target windows-x86_64 tests/codegen/src/union-init-fields.bas -o tests/codegen/unioninitfields.exe
'' ENV: TKO_LIBPATH=build/obj/rtlib/windows-x86_64
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' RUN: tests/codegen/unioninitfields.exe
'' EXPECT-RUN-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT:  1 2 3
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT:  5 5
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT:  1 1 0 2
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT:  1 1 0
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT:  1 1 2
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT:  7 8 9
